Components

Gateway (Node/TS)

Connects to exchange Socket.IO public depth streams (INR book, USDT book for each coin; plus USDT/INR).

Maintains in-memory top-of-book (best bid/ask + volume) and relevant levels (up to N=5 for slippage checks).

Authenticated endpoints: REST order placement/cancel; private user stream for fills/balances.

Sends normalized ticks to engine over UDS (Unix domain socket) using FlatBuffers (or Protobuf).

Arb Engine (Rust)

Holds the market graph and all valid triangles.

On tick, recomputes only affected triangles; outputs OrderBundle decisions if edge exceeds thresholds.

Deterministic decimal math; precision & min-notional enforcement.

Emits metrics and structured logs.

Store

ClickHouse for ticks (top-of-book snapshots), decisions, orders, fills, balances, and P&L.

Write-ahead appenders; no DB in the hot path.

Ops & Observability

Prometheus exporters from gateway and engine.

Grafana dashboards: latency, edge distribution, symbol health, error codes, disconnects.

Alertmanager rules (SLO/SLA).

Data flow (hot path)
Exchange Socket.IO → gateway normalize → UDS frame → engine compute → UDS decision → gateway place orders (REST) → private socket events → gateway state & CH writes

Latency budget (targets)

Socket tick → Node parse: ≤ 1ms

Node → Rust (UDS): ≤ 0.2ms

Engine compute (impacted triangles): ≤ 2ms

Decision → REST order POST: ≤ 1ms

Exchange ack p99 (network/exchange): outside control; monitor & adapt